\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Geometry of the $880$ order-$4$ Magic Gems. (a)~Number of hull vertices ($8$ to $16$; modal value $12$). (b)~Exact hull volume ($155$ distinct values between $58$ and $292/3$). (c)~Sizes of the $352$ combinatorial types (logarithmic scale): $93$ types occur once, $201$ twice, and one type is shared by $32$ squares. (d)--(f)~Three extreme gems, drawn with translucent faces after merging coplanar triangles: the unique $(8,14,8)$ gem (square \#54; the eight interior points are shown in red), a gem with all $16$ points extreme (square \#802, D\"urer's square with its first two rows exchanged and its last two rows exchanged), and the gem of largest volume (square \#379).}}{20}{figure.113}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gem-geometry-880}{{3}{20}{Geometry of the $880$ order-$4$ Magic Gems. (a)~Number of hull vertices ($8$ to $16$; modal value $12$). (b)~Exact hull volume ($155$ distinct values between $58$ and $292/3$). (c)~Sizes of the $352$ combinatorial types (logarithmic scale): $93$ types occur once, $201$ twice, and one type is shared by $32$ squares. (d)--(f)~Three extreme gems, drawn with translucent faces after merging coplanar triangles: the unique $(8,14,8)$ gem (square \#54; the eight interior points are shown in red), a gem with all $16$ points extreme (square \#802, D\"urer's square with its first two rows exchanged and its last two rows exchanged), and the gem of largest volume (square \#379)}{figure.113}{}}
